  <div><strong>Output</strong> Repo + Drive folder + DNS access + all assets in hand; design starts next</div>
</div>

<h2>The kickoff call (30 min)</h2>
<p>Schedule within 5 business days of agreement. Goal: walk through the onboarding form together if they haven't filled it out, capture anything not in writing yet, set the launch date in stone.</p>

<h3>Agenda</h3>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Introductions if needed.</strong> Anyone else who'll have approval power on design (spouse, partner, office manager). Decide who has final say.</li>
  <li><strong>Walk the onboarding form.</strong> If they filled it out, just confirm gaps. If not, fill it together.</li>
  <li><strong>Confirm launch window.</strong> Pick a specific week. Block it on our calendar.</li>
  <li><strong>Asset deadline.</strong> Photos, logo, copy, current-site export. I can't start design without these.</li>
  <li><strong>Communication preferences.</strong> Email vs text vs phone for routine vs urgent. Document in CRM.</li>
  <li><strong>What to expect.</strong> Two design rounds typical, preview link in 7-10 business days, full preview before any code goes live.</li>
</ol>

<h2>Asset checklist</h2>
<p>What I need from them, in order of importance.</p>

<ul class="sop-checklist">
  <li><strong>Logo</strong> &middot; vector preferred (SVG, AI, EPS, PDF). Raster (PNG/JPG) at 1000px+ acceptable. If no logo: schedule logo design as a separate sub-project.</li>
  <li><strong>Brand colors</strong> &middot; hex codes if they have them, or a description ("navy + gold," "earth tones") and I will propose.</li>
  <li><strong>Photos</strong> &middot; 10-30 high-res photos of their work, team, location. iPhone shots are fine if recent. Avoid stock if at all possible.</li>
  <li><strong>Copy / content</strong> &middot; existing site text, About page draft, service descriptions, any awards or credentials. Bullet points OK; I will write it up.</li>
  <li><strong>Customer testimonials</strong> &middot; verbatim quotes if available. First name + city is the minimum attribution I want.</li>
  <li><strong>License + insurance details</strong> &middot; license numbers, BBB / industry certifications, insurance amounts. Builds trust on every page.</li>
  <li><strong>Service areas</strong> &middot; list of cities, counties, or radius from base. Affects how many area pages I build.</li>
  <li><strong>Current website export</strong> &middot; if they have a WordPress site, an export of pages + media. Otherwise just a list of URLs we should preserve / redirect.</li>
  <li><strong>Domain registrar access</strong> &middot; I do not take over their account; we just need them to point DNS or add records. Confirm they know their registrar login.</li>
  <li><strong>Google Business Profile</strong> &middot; URL, current review count. I do not manage GBP, but we wire site schema to match.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Internal provisioning</h2>
<p>Once kickoff is done, set up the project infrastructure. Don't wait for the design phase.</p>

<ul class="sop-checklist">
  <li>Create a private GitHub repo: <code>pikes-peak-{client-slug}</code>.</li>
  <li>Run the new-project scaffold from the <code>new-project</code> skill (in <code>.claude/skills/</code>).</li>
  <li>Create a Drive folder: <code>Clients / {Business Name}</code>. Sub-folders: <code>assets, agreements, invoices, communications</code>.</li>
  <li>Drop the signed agreement in <code>agreements/</code>. Photo of any wet-ink signatures.</li>
  <li>Add the client to the active-clients spreadsheet with: start date, plan, billing day, primary contact.</li>
  <li>Provision Web3Forms access keys. Hard-code into the repo <code>_data/site.js</code>.</li>
  <li>Add their domain to our WHOIS-watch list for renewal monitoring.</li>
  <li>Create a Cloudflare Pages project with the GitHub repo connected. Note the <code>*.pages.dev</code> preview URL.</li>
  <li>Send the kickoff-confirmation email below.</li>
</ul>

